{
  "//": [
    "contrib/antigravity/settings.json.example — shows chaining the panel's",
    "Antigravity status emitter AHEAD of Jordan's existing oh-my-posh",
    "statusline, mirroring how ~/.claude/settings.json already chains",
    "contrib/claude-code/statusline.sh and `oh-my-posh claude` (see",
    "contrib/claude-code/statusline.sh's header for that sibling).",
    "",
    "This merges into ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/settings.json's `statusLine`",
    "key (agy's top-level settings file — NOT hooks.json, which is a",
    "separate file with its own schema; see hooks.json.example in this",
    "directory for the PreInvocation/Stop wiring). The '//' key above is not",
    "part of agy's settings schema — strip it before installing.",
    "",
    "SHIPPED — stage 24b (2026-08-14): contrib/antigravity/statusline.sh now",
    "exists and is verified against a real captured payload (agy 1.1.13).",
    "The quota map's two bucket keys are `gemini-weekly` and `3p-weekly` —",
    "both weekly; there is no 5-hour window, unlike Claude Code's rate",
    "limits. See statusline.sh's own header for the full field mapping and",
    "README.md for the verification transcript.",
    "",
    "Install steps (see README.md for the full install-steps list):",
    "  1. Back up ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/settings.json.",
    "  2. Merge this file's `statusLine.command` into it (agy's own other",
    "     settings keys — colorScheme, enableTelemetry, trustedWorkspaces —",
    "     stay whatever Jordan already has; this file only shows the one key",
    "     that changes).",
    "  3. Confirm both scripts are executable (chmod +x).",
    "",
    "Why `command` reads stdin once and fans it out with printf, rather than",
    "two commands chained with `&&` each reading stdin themselves: stdin is a",
    "stream, not a rewindable buffer — a second command in a shell pipeline",
    "sees an already-drained (empty) stdin if the first one already consumed",
    "it. `~/.claude/settings.json`'s existing Claude Code chain (its",
    "statusLine.command, readable but not editable by this repo) uses exactly",
    "this `payload=$(cat); printf ... | first; printf ... | second` shape for",
    "the same reason — copied here verbatim as the pattern to follow once",
    "statusline.sh exists. `~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/statusline.sh` below is",
    "Jordan's EXISTING oh-my-posh wrapper (the one settings.json already",
    "points statusLine.command at today) — the panel emitter runs first so",
    "its own signal never depends on that script having already run or",
    "exited 0. See README.md: that existing script's own rate-limit lookup",
    "is bugged (falls through to fabricated 0% quota) — worth Jordan's",
    "attention independent of when stage 24b ships."
  ],
  "statusLine": {
    "type": "command",
    "command": "payload=$(cat); printf '%s' \"$payload\" | $HOME/Developer/saola-panel/contrib/antigravity/statusline.sh; printf '%s' \"$payload\" | $HOME/.gemini/antigravity-cli/statusline.sh"
  }
}
